SDCoherentPinout1|SDRAM Coherent Pinout|SDRAM control||||
SDBank1|Bank|SDRAM control||||
SDMemoryDataWidth1|Data size|SDRAM control||||
ColumnBitsNumber1|Number of column address bits|SDRAM control||||
RowBitsNumber1|Number of row address bits|SDRAM control||||
InternalBankNumber1|Internal bank number|SDRAM control||||
CASLatency1|CAS latency|SDRAM control||||Specifies the SDRAM Column Access Strobe (CAS) latency in number of memory clock cycles.
WriteProtection1|Write protection|SDRAM control||||
SDClockPeriod1|SDRAM common clock|SDRAM control||||Specifies the SDRAM clock period for both SDRAM banks and allows disabling the clock before changing the frequency. In this case the SDRAM must be re-initialized. The corresponding bits in the FMC_SDCR2 register are read only.
ReadBurst1|SDRAM common burst read|SDRAM control||||Enables burst read mode. The SDRAM controller anticipates the next read commands during the CAS latency and stores data in the Read FIFO. The corresponding bit in the FMC_SDCR2 register is don't care.
ReadPipeDelay1|SDRAM common read pipe delay|SDRAM control||||Specifies the delay, in HCLK clock cycles, for reading data after CAS latency. The corresponding bits in the FMC_SDCR2 register are read only.
LoadToActiveDelay1|Load mode register to active delay|SDRAM timing in memory clock cycles||1|16|Specifies the delay between a Load Mode Register command and an Active or Refresh command in number of memory clock cycles. If two SDRAM devices are connected, all the accesses performed simultaneously to both devices by the Command Mode register (Load Mode Register command) are issued using the timing parameters configured for Bank 1 (TMRD (Load mode register to active delay) and TRAS (Self-refresh time) timings) in the FMC_SDTR1 register. The TRP (Row precharge delay) and TRC (Row cycle delay) timings are only configured in the FMC_SDTR1 register. If two SDRAM devices are used, the TRP and TRC timings must be programmed with the timings of the slowest device.
ExitSelfRefreshDelay1|Exit self-refresh delay|SDRAM timing in memory clock cycles||1|16|Specifies the delay from releasing the Self-refresh command to issuing the Activate command in number of memory clock cycles. If two SDRAM devices are used, the FMC_SDTR1 and FMC_SDTR2 registers must be programmed with the same Exit Self-refresh Delay corresponding to the slowest SDRAM device.
SelfRefreshTime1|Self-refresh time|SDRAM timing in memory clock cycles||1|16|Specifies the minimum Self-refresh period in number of memory clock cycles.
RowCycleDelay1|SDRAM common row cycle delay|SDRAM timing in memory clock cycles||1|16|Specifies the delay between the Refresh command and the Activate command, as well as the delay between two consecutive Refresh commands. It is expressed in number of memory clock cycles. The Row Cycle Delay is only configured in the FMC_SDTR1 register. If two SDRAM devices are used, the Row Cycle Delay must be programmed with the timings of the slowest device.
WriteRecoveryTime1|Write recovery time|SDRAM timing in memory clock cycles||=MAX(1,MAX(SelfRefreshTime1-RCDDelay1,RowCycleDelay1-RCDDelay1-RPDelay1))|16|Specifies the delay between a Write and a Precharge command in number of memory clock cycles. WriteRecoveryTime must satisfy the following constraints: 1: WriteRecoveryTime >= SelfRefreshTime - RowToColumnDelay, 2: WriteRecoveryTime >= RowCycleDelay - RowToColumnDelay - RowPrechargeDelay. If two SDRAM devices are used, the FMC_SDTR1 and FMC_SDTR2 registers must be programmed with the same Write Recovery Time corresponding to the slowest SDRAM device.
RPDelay1|SDRAM common row precharge delay|SDRAM timing in memory clock cycles||1|16|Specifies the delay between a Precharge command and another command in number of memory clock cycles. The Row Precharge Delay is only configured in the FMC_SDTR1 register. If two SDRAM devices are used, the Row Precharge Delay must be programmed with the timing of the slowest device.
RCDDelay1|Row to column delay|SDRAM timing in memory clock cycles||1|16|Specifies the delay between the Activate command and a Read/Write command in number of memory clock cycles.
SDCoherentPinout2|SDRAM Coherent Pinout|SDRAM control||||
SDBank2|Bank|SDRAM control||||
SDMemoryDataWidth2|Data size|SDRAM control||||
ColumnBitsNumber2|Number of column address bits|SDRAM control||||
RowBitsNumber2|Number of row address bits|SDRAM control||||
InternalBankNumber2|Internal bank number|SDRAM control||||
CASLatency2|CAS latency|SDRAM control||||Specifies the SDRAM Column Access Strobe (CAS) latency in number of memory clock cycles.
WriteProtection2|Write protection|SDRAM control||||
SDClockPeriod2|SDRAM common clock|SDRAM control||||Specifies the SDRAM clock period for both SDRAM banks and allows disabling the clock before changing the frequency. In this case the SDRAM must be re-initialized. The corresponding bits in the FMC_SDCR2 register are read only.
ReadBurst2|SDRAM common burst read|SDRAM control||||Enables burst read mode. The SDRAM controller anticipates the next read commands during the CAS latency and stores data in the Read FIFO. The corresponding bit in the FMC_SDCR2 register is don't care.
ReadPipeDelay2|SDRAM common read pipe delay|SDRAM control||||Specifies the delay, in HCLK clock cycles, for reading data after CAS latency. The corresponding bits in the FMC_SDCR2 register are read only.
LoadToActiveDelay2|Load mode register to active delay|SDRAM timing in memory clock cycles||1|16|Specifies the delay between a Load Mode Register command and an Active or Refresh command in number of memory clock cycles. If two SDRAM devices are connected, all the accesses performed simultaneously to both devices by the Command Mode register (Load Mode Register command) are issued using the timing parameters configured for Bank 1 (TMRD (Load mode register to active delay) and TRAS (Self-refresh time) timings) in the FMC_SDTR1 register. The TRP (Row precharge delay) and TRC (Row cycle delay) timings are only configured in the FMC_SDTR1 register. If two SDRAM devices are used, the TRP and TRC timings must be programmed with the timings of the slowest device.
ExitSelfRefreshDelay2|Exit self-refresh delay|SDRAM timing in memory clock cycles||1|16|Specifies the delay from releasing the Self-refresh command to issuing the Activate command in number of memory clock cycles. If two SDRAM devices are used, the FMC_SDTR1 and FMC_SDTR2 registers must be programmed with the same Exit Self-refresh Delay corresponding to the slowest SDRAM device.
SelfRefreshTime2|Self-refresh time|SDRAM timing in memory clock cycles||1|16|Specifies the minimum Self-refresh period in number of memory clock cycles.
RowCycleDelay2|SDRAM common row cycle delay|SDRAM timing in memory clock cycles||1|16|Specifies the delay between the Refresh command and the Activate command, as well as the delay between two consecutive Refresh commands. It is expressed in number of memory clock cycles. The Row Cycle Delay is only configured in the FMC_SDTR1 register. If two SDRAM devices are used, the Row Cycle Delay must be programmed with the timings of the slowest device.
WriteRecoveryTime2|Write recovery time|SDRAM timing in memory clock cycles||=MAX(1,MAX(SelfRefreshTime2-RCDDelay2,RowCycleDelay2-RCDDelay2-RPDelay2))|16|Specifies the delay between a Write and a Precharge command in number of memory clock cycles. WriteRecoveryTime must satisfy the following constraints: 1: WriteRecoveryTime >= SelfRefreshTime - RowToColumnDelay, 2: WriteRecoveryTime >= RowCycleDelay - RowToColumnDelay - RowPrechargeDelay. If two SDRAM devices are used, the FMC_SDTR1 and FMC_SDTR2 registers must be programmed with the same Write Recovery Time corresponding to the slowest SDRAM device.
RPDelay2|SDRAM common row precharge delay|SDRAM timing in memory clock cycles||1|16|Specifies the delay between a Precharge command and another command in number of memory clock cycles. The Row Precharge Delay is only configured in the FMC_SDTR1 register. If two SDRAM devices are used, the Row Precharge Delay must be programmed with the timing of the slowest device.
RCDDelay2|Row to column delay|SDRAM timing in memory clock cycles||1|16|Specifies the delay between the Activate command and a Read/Write command in number of memory clock cycles.

